		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4559&amp;p=33932#p33932"><![CDATA[
Folks:<br><br>I have both Simplex and Duplex MMDVM hotspots built upon Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W boards with eBay sourced Hats. I use the WPSD software rather than the traditional Pi-star, as WPSD has more features, and is most importantly, actively maintained.<br><br>Both of these configurations work just fine, and although I have more than one DMR radio, I typically operate one at a time, on a single talkgroup.<br><br>I'm curious what others think the advantages / disadvantages of simplex vs. duplex MMDVM boards / hotspots might be?<br><br>Please discuss........<br><br><br><br>73<br><br>AL<br>K5FQ<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7118">k5fq</a> — Tue Nov 05, 2024 3:08 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
